# tally 2.2.1, OPERATIONS §2.1 (229.1, 233.5, R20 clause 1): a scenario file's own ask refused alone prints its line in
# run in its place by id (q_gone); the refused scenario's line prints once, first; an ask in its world with as known
# after on (q_bad) is covered by that line, no REQ-CLOCK (S-233.5). tally 2.2 printed nothing for q_gone.
=== options exit=0
=== b.tally
model bob
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "b card"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input pay: money PLN

def twice: money PLN = pay + pay at reader

ask q: twice law 2026-03-01


version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 3 000.00 PLN "the card"
=== sb.tally
scenario sb over bob
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version lower
  cite card
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-02
  replace pay = 2 000.00 PLN "a cut"

ask q_sb: twice in sb law 2026-03-01

ask q_gone: twice in nowhere law 2026-03-01
=== sbad.tally
scenario sbad over bob
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

version lower2
  cite card
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-02
  replace pay = 2 000.00 USD "a cut"

ask q_bad: twice in sbad law 2026-03-01 as known 2026-06-01
=== expect
scenario sbad: refused: LOAD-UNIT 2 000.00 USD and money PLN have different units (sbad.tally:9)
q: 6 000.00 PLN
  law date 2026-03-01, cut 2026-03-01
q_gone: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ask q_gone names nowhere, neither the model nor a loaded scenario (sb.tally:13)
q_sb: 4 000.00 PLN
  world: sb
  law date 2026-03-01, cut 2026-03-01
